ffmpeg-dmo (@VERSION@) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Show a side by side or top and bottom Matroska track whose display
    size is the whole frame at the shape the file declares (ORDER 577).
    The Matroska demuxer doubled the display width of every side by side
    and column interleaved track, and the height of every top and bottom
    and row interleaved one (FFmpeg ec83efd4d3, 2015), so a film whose
    two views are whole pictures, 2560x720 declared 2560x720, showed
    views of 32:9. The display size is now read as one plane (RFC 9559
    section 18.10) only when a view of the frame as declared cannot be a
    whole picture: narrower than 4:3 side by side, 8:3 or wider stacked.
    Patch 0074; patch 0075 adds the FATE test
    fate-matroska-stereo-display-size, which needs no sample.
  * Built on +stereo3d12. +stereo3d13 (ORDER 61c) was never published
    and is not in this version.

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  @DATE@
